# Preserve Python imports (dedupe only)

Do **not** remove Python imports because they look unused (static analysis false positives, re-exports, side effects, TYPE_CHECKING, notebooks, optional deps, etc.).

Only clean up **literal duplicates**: repeated identical imports, or overlapping names from the same module that can be merged into one statement.

## ✅ Allowed — dedupe / merge duplicates

```python
# Before
from typing import List, Set, Tuple
import numpy as np
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np
from typing import Tuple
from typing import Sequence

# After
from typing import List, Set, Tuple, Sequence
import numpy as np
import pandas as pd
```

## ❌ Not allowed — removing “unused” imports

Do not delete an import solely because nothing in the visible file references it. Leave it unless the user asks to prune unused imports, or it is a literal duplicate as above.

## Rules

- Keep imports that appear unused
- Remove only exact duplicate import lines (same module + same binding)
- When the same `from module import ...` appears more than once, merge names into a single import
- Do not reorder or restyle the whole import block while deduping unless needed for the merge
